      {
        "category": "Physical",
        "description": "A state of mind over matter that slows the metabolism to such a degree that it creates a temporary state of suspended animation, simulating death. Without hospital facilities, even a medical doctor is likely to believe the character is dead (1-89% likelihood). The effects of drugs, toxins and chemicals are slowed to a crawl, doing minimal damage or effect, but will take full effect the instant the death trance is stopped (unless treatment is administered first). While in the death-like state, the psychic can not be roused or respond to any type of stimulation, including psychic probes. This means he is incapable of attacking or defending himself in any way until the trance is broken.",
        "id": "death-trance",
        "name": "Death Trance",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "id": "metadata-0",
            "name": "Range",
            "source": {
              "book": "Rifts Ultimate Edition",
              "section": "Psionic Powers: Death Trance"
            },
            "text": "Self."
          },
          {
            "id": "metadata-1",
            "name": "Duration",
            "source": {
              "book": "Rifts Ultimate Edition",
              "section": "Psionic Powers: Death Trance"
            },
            "text": "As long as the psychic senses he must feign death, up to a maximum of four days."
          },
          {
            "id": "metadata-2",
            "name": "I.S.P.",
            "source": {
              "book": "Rifts Ultimate Edition",
              "section": "Psionic Powers: Death Trance"
            },
            "text": "1, because physical psychics find it easy to control their bodies."
          }
        ],
        "source": {
          "book": "Rifts Ultimate Edition",
          "section": "Psionic Powers: Death Trance"
        },
        "tags": [
          "Physical"
        ]
      },
